      "question": "In the Buddhist doctrine of Dependent Origination (*Pratītyasamutpāda* / *Dvādaśāṅga-bhavacakra*, as codified in the *Pratītyasamutpādasūtra* and Vasubandhu’s *Abhidharmakośa* III), the twelve links span three temporal lives (past, present, future).\n\nMatch the specific Nidānas in **Column I** with their precise psychological-existential definition in **Column II**, and their temporal life allocation in **Column III**:\n\n| Column I (Nidāna) | Column II (Existential/Psychological Function) | Column III (Temporal Life) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **P. Saṁskāra** | 1. The six cognitive-sensory domains (five physical senses + mind-base) emerging in the embryo. | i. Past Life (*Atīta-janma*) |\n| **Q. Nāmarūpa** | 2. Volitional karmic formations (bodily, verbal, mental) conditioned by fundamental ignorance. | ii. Present Life (*Pratyutpanna-janma*) |\n| **R. Ṣaḍāyatana** | 3. The psychosomatic organism (mental factors + physical embryonic matrix) taking shape in the womb. | iii. Future Life (*Anāgata-janma*) |\n| **S. Jāti** | 4. Re-birth / the emergence of the five aggregates anew in a future existence. | |\n\nChoose the correct matching code:",
