      "correct_option": "A",
      "correct_answer_text": "A) Both (A) and (R) are true, and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).",
      "grounding": "In Īśvarakṛṣṇa’s *Sāṁkhyakārikā* (verses 22–25) and Vācaspati Miśra’s *Tattvakaumudī*:\n- The evolutionary lineage proceeds:\n  $$\\text{Prakṛti} \\rightarrow \\text{Mahat (Buddhi)} \\rightarrow \\text{Ahaṁkāra}.$$\n- *Ahaṁkāra* branches into a dual evolutionary stream under the influence of the guṇas:\n  1. From **Sāttvika Ahaṁkāra** (conjoined with Rajas, termed *Vaikṛta*): arise the 11 organs (mind, 5 sensory organs, 5 motor organs).\n  2. From **Tāmasika Ahaṁkāra** (conjoined with Rajas, termed *Bhūtādi*): arise the **5 Tanmātras** (*śabda, sparśa, rūpa, rasa, gandha*).\n  3. From the **5 Tanmātras**: arise the **5 Mahābhūtas** (*ākāśa, vāyu, tejas, ap, pṛthivī*).\n- **Reason (R)**: The *Tanmātras* are infra-atomic, unparticularized potentials of matter (*aviśeṣa*). They are subtle, sound-in-itself, touch-in-itself, devoid of gross sensory distress or delight (*aśānta-aghora-amūḍha*). Gross elements (*mahābhūtas*) are composite, dense, and particularized (*viśeṣa*). In accordance with *Satkāryavāda*, gross physical mass cannot emerge directly from pure subjective apperception (*ahaṁkāra*) without the condensation of potential energy through the *tāmasika* continuum of *bhūtādi* into subtle proto-material fields (*tanmātras*). Thus, (R) provides the definitive metaphysical rationale for (A).",
      "distractor_analysis": "- **Option B is incorrect**: (R) is not a disconnected truth; it provides the exact structural logic for the insertion of the *tanmātra* layer in Sāṁkhya cosmology.\n- **Options C and D are incorrect**: Both statements are directly derived from the canonical text of the *Sāṁkhyakārikā*.\n\n---",
