      "question": "Given below are two statements: one is labelled as **Assertion (A)** and the other is labelled as **Reason (R)**:\n\n**Assertion (A)**: In Advaita Vedānta, upon the dawn of liberating knowledge (*Brahmasākṣātkāra*), the enlightened sage (*Jīvanmukta*) continues to live in the physical body until the exhaustion of his **Prārabdha-karma**, even though his **Sañcita-karma** (accumulated past karmas) and **Āgāmī-karma** (future karmas) are completely incinerated.  \n**Reason (R)**: Because *Prārabdha-karma* has already commenced its operational momentum (*pravṛtta-phala*) to generate the present physical embodiment, sensory apparatus, and lifespan, it must run its course to natural termination, like an arrow already released from the archer’s bow (*mukteṣuvat*) or the continuing rotation of a potter’s wheel (*cakrabhramavat*) after the potter has ceased to spin it.\n\nIn light of the above statements, choose the correct option:",
