      "format_type": "A",
      "question": "In *\"On the Moral and Legal Status of Abortion\"* (1973), Mary Anne Warren demonstrates that traditional anti-abortion arguments commit the fallacy of **Equivocation** on the term **\"human\"**. How does Warren unpack this equivocation, and what five criteria does she propose for membership in the **moral community (Personhood)**?",
