          "question": "- **Assertion (A)**: In Jaina ontology, Time (*Kala*) is categorized as an immaterial substance (*arupavat-dravya*) alongside *Dharma*, *Adharma*, and *Akasa*, but is distinguished from them as an *anastikaya-dravya*.\n- **Reason (R)**: *Kala* does not possess spatial extension (*pradesa*) or bodily manifoldness, existing as atomic temporal units (*kalāṇu*) that do not combine to form extensive spatial configurations.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer:",
