          "domain": "Classical Indian Philosophy (Post-Sankara Vedanta)",
          "format_type": "Assertion-Reason",
          "question": "- **Assertion (A)**: In post-Sankara Advaita Vedanta, the Bhamati school of Vacaspati Misra and the Vivarana school of Prakasatman diverge fundamentally on the ontological locus (*asraya*) of Ignorance (*Avidya*).\n- **Reason (R)**: Vacaspati Misra holds that the individual empirical soul (*Jiva*) is the locus (*asraya*) of Avidya while Brahman is its object (*visaya*), whereas Prakasatman argues that Brahman alone is both the locus (*asraya*) and the object (*visaya*) of Avidya, since the Jiva is itself a product of Avidya.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer:",
