          "correct_option": "A",
          "reference": "Ramanuja, *Sribhasya*, Mahasiddhanta section (*Saptavidha Anupapatti*).",
          "grounding": "Ramanuja levels seven major logical/ontological objections (*anupapattis*) against the Advaitic concept of Avidya:\n  1. *Asrayanupapatti*: An absence of locus. Avidya cannot reside in the Jiva (who is created by avidya) nor in Brahman (pure knowledge). (Matches 3).\n  2. *Tirodhananupapatti*: Impossibility of concealment. If avidya conceals Brahman, since Brahman's nature is self-luminous knowledge, concealment means destruction of Brahman's essential nature. (Matches 1).\n  3. *Anirvacaniyanupapatti*: Indefinability is untenable. Everything is either real or unreal; an indeterminate third entity violates the law of excluded middle. (Matches 2).\n  4. *Nivartakanupapatti*: Non-removability. Knowledge of an attributeless Brahman cannot remove ignorance, because all knowledge is determinate and qualified (*savisesa*). (Matches 4).\n  - Hence, the matching sequence is a-3, b-1, c-2, d-4.",
