          "question": "- **Assertion (A)**: In Plato's *Theaetetus*, Socrates decisively refutes the third candidate definition of knowledge—namely, that knowledge is \"true judgment accompanied by an account\" (*doxa alethes meta logou*).\n- **Reason (R)**: To give an account (*logos*) must mean either analyzing a complex into its elements, stating its differentiating feature, or expressing thought through speech; in each case, the account either reduces to unanalyzable unknowable elements (Dream of Socrates) or presupposes epistemic knowledge of the differentiating mark, generating vicious circularity.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer:",
