          "grounding": "Davidson reconciles the physical causality of the mental with the autonomy of reason through three premises:\n  1. *Principle of Causal Interaction*: At least some mental events interact causally with physical events.\n  2. *Principle of the Nomological Character of Causality*: Where there is causality, there must be strict deterministic laws.\n  3. *Anomalism of the Mental*: There are no strict deterministic laws on the basis of which mental events can be predicted and explained.\n  Davidson's resolution is **Anomalous Monism**: Every concrete mental event is identical with a physical event (Token Physicalism). However, because mental concepts are governed by normative constraints of rationality and coherence, they cannot be systematically correlated by bridge laws with physical types (rejection of Type Physicalism).",
