          "grounding": "- Statement I is correct: *Aufhebung* is the motor of dialectic, meaning to negate, preserve, and elevate.\n  - Statement II is correct: In the *Philosophy of Right*, *Sittlichkeit* (Ethical Life) is dialectically structured into: (1) The Family (immediate substantial unity), (2) Civil Society (*die bürgerliche Gesellschaft*, the system of needs and particularity), and (3) The State (the concrete universal synthesis of individual freedom and ethical community).\n  - Statement III is correct: In the Preface, Hegel articulates his famous double-dictum: \"What is rational is actual; and what is actual is rational.\"\n  - Statement IV is FALSE: Hegel did NOT advocate a return to feudalism! He regarded the modern constitutional state (with rule of law, individual rights, civil society, and constitutional monarchy) as the highest achievement of Objective Spirit, welcoming the core principles of the French Revolution while criticizing the Terror.\n  Therefore, Statements I, II, and III are correct.",
